CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ 90 seconds: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ commuted: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Was KNOWNBUG: mixed-period duration operator+ (minutes + seconds)
returned nondet ([time.duration.nonmember]).  Three stacked front-end
defects, all fixed:
1. [temp.deduct]/5 + [basic.scope.temp]/2: deducing the duration
   converting constructor bound/conflict-checked same-short-name
   parameters of UNRELATED enclosing templates (operator+'s _Period2 vs
   the constructor's own _Period2), and the flat-map short-name
   substitution baked the caller's binding into the deduced signature.
   Deduction is now restricted to the deduced template's own parameters
   (current_deduction_parameters / template_map.deduction_parameters).
   Also made typecheck_type's cpp_name handling exception-safe: a failed
   SFINAE resolution no longer guts the stored declaration's name node
   ([temp.deduct]/8: substitution failure has no lasting effect).
2. [temp.inst]/5 + [expr.const]: the constexpr _S_gcd called in the
   DEFAULT TEMPLATE ARGUMENTS of duration's __divide member alias sat
   unconverted in the deferred method-body queue; its definition is now
   instantiated on demand (convert_deferred_method_now).
3. [stmt.dowhile] + [dcl.init]: the constexpr evaluator did not execute
   do-while loops, dropped declaration initializers, and skipped
   expression-statement assignments, so _S_gcd evaluated to garbage and
   __is_harmonic degraded to false, deleting the converting constructor.
See cpp11_fn_template_param_shadow for the minimal header-free layer-1
reproducer.
